PROJECT DIRECTIVE
============================================================

You are continuing development of an existing, playable game.

Your responsibility is to transform Wispwake from a functional
2D platformer with a largely static painted background into
a visually rich, atmospheric, living fantasy world.

This milestone has THREE equally important objectives:

1. Redesign Nima and Pip to closely match the quality and
   appearance of their original character concept artwork.

2. Transform the current environment into a richly layered,
   animated, living forest.

3. Replace the visibly primitive and repetitive platform
   presentation with sophisticated organic environmental art.

There is also one important product decision:

REMOVE THE AI ART GENERATION INTERFACE FROM THE ACTUAL GAME.

Google AI Studio is our development environment and artwork
production workspace.

Wispwake is the finished player-facing game.

Players must never see AI generation controls, model names,
API configuration, or developer asset-generation interfaces.

Do not create a new project.

Do not replace the existing gameplay architecture.

Do not casually rewrite successful systems.

Do not sacrifice gameplay quality to achieve visual complexity.

